    {
      "id": "surface-invariants",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Invariants",
      "position": {
        "x": 380,
        "y": -640
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 320,
      "data": {
        "title": "Invariants",
        "body": "**What makes this thing a Surface, specifically?**\n\n- **A Surface is a chain face → face → … → Glyph.** The root's `surface` edge points at the first face; each face points at the next with a `next-face` edge; the last points at a Glyph. Every Surface begins with a face and ends in a Glyph. A graph that should show as just a glyph uses a face that renders glyph-shaped artwork (it need not be named Icon), then ends its chain with its ordinary Glyph.\n- **The `surface` edge is the Surface's only identity.** It carries `data.surfaceId`. Rename it there; delete the edge to remove the Surface (its faces stay in the graph, in no Surface); if two edges share an id the first wins. Which faces belong to a Surface is decided by the chain, so a face carries no `surfaceId` of its own.\n- A graph that draws no `surface` edges has no Surface, and shows only its Glyph.\n- A Surface's chain is **open-ended**: `authoredViewResolution()` lets a face claim any continuous resolution value, so a chain can have three rungs or thirty.\n- A host resolves a graph by first selecting a Surface, then resolving richest-fitting *within that Surface's own chain* — never mixing rungs from two Surfaces into one decision.\n- **A Surface chooses what renders inside the graph's frame. It never resizes the frame, reflows neighbors or moves the camera.**\n- **An explicit request wins.** A host that names a Surface gets it. Without a request, `root.defaultSurfaceId` answers (else the first Surface). A Surface the host cannot render anything of is never chosen: capability filters, and never decides.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "definitionKey": "page-section",
        "_classBinding": {
