    {
      "id": "surface-contract",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Contract",
      "position": {
        "x": -180,
        "y": -280
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 320,
      "data": {
        "title": "Contract",
        "body": "**What data belongs to it?**\n\nIn the app now:\n\n```text\nsurface edge      root -> first face            data.surfaceId = the Surface's id\nnext-face         face -> next face, last face -> Glyph\nroot.defaultSurfaceId           which Surface answers when a host does not ask\nface payload      names its host: node.web.detail, editor.web -> web; node.3d.detail -> 3d\n                  (a face that names none is written for any host)\n```\n\n`root.surfaces[]` is **not** where presentation Surfaces live. It keeps its entries of kind `export` and `port`, which serve exports and exposed Ports; the two purposes no longer share a record.\n\n**Not built:** a host declaring its own *context* so that context picks the default Surface. Today a host names the Surface it wants, or takes the default, and may pass what it can render (`hosts`) so it is never handed something it cannot draw.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "definitionKey": "page-section",
