    {
      "id": "surface-ports",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Ports and Relationships",
      "position": {
        "x": 380,
        "y": -280
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 320,
      "data": {
        "title": "Ports and Relationships",
        "body": "**What semantic relationships does it expose?**\n\nNone directly — Surface is not a node type. There is no `type:'surface'` node to drop on a canvas. It is drawn as edges:\n\n- The root's `surfaces` port (repeatable): one `surface` edge per Surface, to the Surface's first face, carrying its id.\n- `next-face` edges down the chain, ending at a Glyph. Faces have a `sequence-in` and a `sequence-out` port; a Glyph has a `sequence-in`.\n\nA second Surface needs no new vocabulary on the root, only another `surface` edge.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "definitionKey": "page-section",
