      "data": {
        "title": "Explicitly Not Part of This Primitive",
        "body": "- Surface does not replace faces, Content, or Glyph. It orders and scopes them; it doesn't render in their place.\n- Surface is not an export. A Surface is about which *faces* a graph offers to a host; an export is about which *classes or resources* a graph offers an importer. They used to share the `root.surfaces[]` array; presentation Surfaces are now edges, and that array keeps only the export and port entries.\n- Surface does not negotiate beyond: explicit request, then the default, then the first Surface the host can render. A \"closest available\" match between related contexts is out of scope.\n- Surface does not define what a map, a 3D scene or any other host does with what it receives — only that it can ask for and receive a chain scoped to it. The renderers are not part of this primitive.\n- Surface does not decide the graph's frame. That comes from the root and its ground.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "definitionKey": "page-section",
